1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:03,687
Clinical trials require accurate,
standardized, and traceable data.

2
00:00:03,737 --> 00:00:08,097
Converting a clinical Protocol into an
eCRF remains highly manual.

3
00:00:08,147 --> 00:00:11,198
Teams identify required data, design
fields, define

4
00:00:11,248 --> 00:00:14,736
validation rules, and map them to CDISC
CDASH.

5
00:00:14,786 --> 00:00:19,581
Even a small amendment can affect forms,
mappings, and downstream analysis.

6
00:00:20,131 --> 00:00:22,617
We created Codex Clinical Form Studio.

7
00:00:22,667 --> 00:00:25,981
It is a reusable Plugin composed of
specialized

8
00:00:26,031 --> 00:00:28,517
Skills, not a single form-generating
prompt.

9
00:00:28,567 --> 00:00:33,125
After a user uploads a Protocol, an
Orchestrator Skill coordinates analysis,

10
00:00:33,175 --> 00:00:36,489
design, CDASH mapping, clinical review,
testing, and deployment.

11
00:00:36,539 --> 00:00:40,268
Every stage has defined input, output, and
human approval.

12
00:00:40,818 --> 00:00:43,845
The Orchestrator invokes the Protocol
Analysis Skill,

13
00:00:43,895 --> 00:00:46,921
while GPT-5.6 provides medical and logical
reasoning.

14
00:00:46,971 --> 00:00:50,863
GPT-5.6 identifies forms, fields, data
types, units, required conditions,

15
00:00:50,913 --> 00:00:55,236
options, and validation rules, then
converts them into structured YAML.

16
00:00:55,286 --> 00:00:58,313
YAML becomes the single source of truth.

17
00:00:58,363 --> 00:01:01,822
Clinical users can review it in a web

18
00:01:01,872 --> 00:01:04,466
interface instead of editing application
code.

19
00:01:05,016 --> 00:01:07,589
Clinical users modify fields, required
conditions,

20
00:01:07,639 --> 00:01:09,784
numeric limits, and selectable options.

21
00:01:09,834 --> 00:01:11,549
The Orchestrator then invokes

22
00:01:11,599 --> 00:01:13,315
the CDASH Mapping Skill.

23
00:01:13,365 --> 00:01:16,796
GPT-5.6 evaluates each field in its
Protocol context,

24
00:01:16,846 --> 00:01:19,848
ranks CDASH candidates, and explains its
recommendations.

25
00:01:19,898 --> 00:01:24,615
AI suggests, but the clinical professional
makes the final mapping decision.

26
00:01:29,016 --> 00:01:31,517
After approval, the Form Generation Skill

27
00:01:31,567 --> 00:01:33,652
converts YAML into standardized JSON.

28
00:01:33,702 --> 00:01:37,454
The JSON-to-HTML renderer generates an
executable eCRF with controls,

29
00:01:37,504 --> 00:01:40,423
required settings, allowed values, ranges,
and validation.

30
00:01:40,473 --> 00:01:44,642
The form first enters a validation
environment for clinical review.

31
00:01:49,016 --> 00:01:52,600
Codex turns the approved specification
into maintainable engineering work.

32
00:01:52,650 --> 00:01:55,836
The Orchestrator directs Codex to update
the application,

33
00:01:55,886 --> 00:01:58,276
generate database migrations, create
pytest and

34
00:01:58,326 --> 00:02:01,512
Playwright tests, and validate in a real
browser.

35
00:02:01,562 --> 00:02:05,146
When a test fails, Codex traces YAML, the
renderer,

36
00:02:05,196 --> 00:02:08,382
or the application, corrects the issue,
and retests.

37
00:02:15,016 --> 00:02:18,217
When a new Protocol version arrives, the
Version

38
00:02:18,267 --> 00:02:20,668
Comparison Skill compares both YAML
specifications.

39
00:02:20,718 --> 00:02:23,918
It identifies added, removed, and modified
fields, including

40
00:02:23,968 --> 00:02:27,169
required conditions, validation rules,
options, and CDASH mappings.

41
00:02:27,219 --> 00:02:30,420
This creates a traceable record of each
amendment.

42
00:02:30,970 --> 00:02:32,626
GPT-5.6 interprets complex Protocols

43
00:02:32,676 --> 00:02:34,746
and reasons about CDISC mappings.

44
00:02:34,796 --> 00:02:37,280
Codex implements the application, writes
tests,

45
00:02:37,330 --> 00:02:40,228
fixes failures, and prepares GitHub pull
requests.

46
00:02:40,278 --> 00:02:43,176
After clinical approval and QA, the CI/CD

47
00:02:43,226 --> 00:02:45,295
pipeline deploys the validated eCRF.

48
00:02:45,345 --> 00:02:49,899
Codex Clinical Form Studio packages the
workflow into a reusable, testable

49
00:02:49,949 --> 00:02:54,089
Plugin. Human approval remains required at
every critical clinical decision.
